# What the web image's build may see: only what it needs. An allowlist, so a file added at the
# root later (a credentials export, scratch notes, a local env file) never reaches the build
# layers. It also keeps the context small: .next alone is gigabytes. Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# from any .env file it finds and copies .env and .env.production into the standalone output, so
# the Dockerfile fails the build if an env file gets through anyway (docs/DECISIONS.md VPS-13).
*

!src
!public
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!next.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!postcss.config.mjs

# Never an environment file, even inside an allowed folder.
**/.env
**/.env.*
